  "notes": "Arabian Cement Company (ticker 3010, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/423_0_2026-02-23...). Auditor: Ernst & Young Professional Services (Ahmed Ibrahim Reda, licence 356); unqualified opinion, dated Jeddah 19 February 2026. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 15 February 2026G (27 Sha'aban 1447H) - Note 39. Amounts are presented in SAR thousands (scale 1000) except per-share data; the primary statements and notes are digital text in the filed PDF (only the auditor's signature page is a scanned image). Consolidated group with a non-controlling interest (its cement subsidiary in Jordan). **IFRS 5 - discontinued operations:** the Group presents a 'Profit for the year from discontinuing operations' line (SAR 6,839k FY2025 / 7,828k FY2024) separately below 'Profit for the year from continuing operations'. The reported 'Profit before zakat and income tax from continuing operations' (SAR 198,938k) and the zakat/income-tax charge are continuing-operations only, so income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is NOT carried; instead continuing_operations_income (SAR 160,736k / 156,384k) + discontinued_operations_income (SAR 6,839k / 7,828k) are carried and net_income (SAR 167,575k / 164,212k) is checked as continuing + discontinued. income_taxes_and_zakat combines the 'Zakat' (SAR -20,439k) and 'Income Tax' (SAR -17,763k) lines. There is also a 'Non-current asset held for sale' of SAR 43,362k at 31 December 2025 (nil FY2024) which the issuer presents INSIDE the total current-assets subtotal (SAR 1,062,561k + 43,362k = 1,105,923k) with no matching liabilities-held-for-sale line, so assets_held_for_sale is carried and the current-assets / total-assets identities hold with it included. investment_property_value is 'Investment property'; long_term_investments is 'Financial assets at fair value through OCI'; other_reserves combines the statutory reserve, general reserve, foreign-currency-translation reserve and the FVOCI fair-value reserve (the statutory and general reserves - SAR 500,000k + 95,000k - were transferred to retained earnings during FY2025 under the new Companies Law, per Note 1, so FY2025 other_reserves is just the two negative reserve balances); additional_paid_in_capital is 'Share Premium'; provisions is the 'Rehabilitation provision' (quarry restoration); long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current portions of 'Long-term loans and facilities'; deferred_tax_assets / deferred_tax_liabilities are carried; lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the reported lease-liability portions; other_current_liabilities is 'Dividends payable'. On the P&L: dividend_income is 'Dividends from financial assets at fair value through OCI'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Share of profit from equity accounted investments'; other_income is 'Other income, net'. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E depreciation, intangible-asset amortization and right-of-use-asset amortization; capex combines 'Additions in property, plant and equipment' and 'Additions in intangible assets'; interest_paid is 'Financial charges paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'; debt_issued is 'Proceeds from term loans'; debt_repaid is 'Repayments of term borrowings'; lease_payments is 'Repayments of lease liabilities'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'; the cash-flow statement has no FX-on-cash line and its closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 6-7, profit or loss 8, comprehensive income 9, changes in equity 10-11, cash flows 12-13.",
